Implement user story SKY-004-impl: Implement Express REST API server with /health, /search, /cheapest, and static dashboard

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts — an Express HTTP server that exposes: (1) GET /health → { status: 'ok', uptime: number }, (2) GET /search?from=LHR&to=JFK&date=2026-08-01&adults=1 → { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: string }, (3) GET /cheapest?from=LHR&to=JFK&date=2026-08-01 → the single cheapest FlightResult or 404 JSON { error: string } if none found, (4) GET / → serves src/public/index.html by reading the file at runtime. Server reads PORT from env (default 3000); reads RAPIDAPI_KEY from env and passes to SkyscannerClient. If RAPIDAPI_KEY is absent at startup all API routes return 503; /health and / are never gated. Depends on SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Express app is created with JSON body parsing and CORS middleware enabled
- GET /health returns { status: 'ok', uptime: <number> } with 200 status
- GET / reads src/public/index.html from disk at runtime and serves it with Content-Type text/html (404 if file missing)
- GET /search validates required query params `from` and `to`; `date` defaults to today; `adults` defaults to 1; returns { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: string } with 200
- GET /search returns 400 with { error: string } when `from` or `to` is missing
- GET /cheapest validates `from` and `to` required; returns single cheapest FlightResult (200) or 404 { error: string } when no flights found
- When RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent, /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: string }; /health and / are never gated
- Server listens on PORT from env (default 3000) and exports the app instance for testing





